# 5. Dimension expansion may therefore be quotient refinement

This is where today's mathematics becomes particularly powerful.

Suppose at time \(t\):

$$
\sim_t
$$

is the current observational equivalence.

Then later we discover a new required distinction \(d_{new}\).

The new relation becomes:

$$
\sim_{t+1}
=
\sim_t\cap\sim_{d_{new}}.
$$

Therefore:

$$
\boxed{
\sim_{t+1}\subseteq\sim_t.
}
$$

So the quotient changes from:

$$
\mathcal S/\sim_t
$$

to:

$$
\mathcal S/\sim_{t+1}.
$$

The new quotient is **finer**.

That gives us a rigorous mathematical interpretation of:

> "The coordinate system itself has expanded."

It may not literally mean vector-space dimension increased.

It can mean:

$$
\boxed{
\text{the observational equivalence became finer}.
}
$$

This is a much stronger formulation.

