# 6. And dimension reduction becomes quotient coarsening

Conversely, if a distinction is determined to be irrelevant or redundant, then the representation may stop preserving it.

The document currently writes:

$$
\mathcal D_{t+1}
=
\mathcal D_t\setminus\{D_3\}.
$$



But mathematically we should not immediately identify that with deletion of information.

Instead there are at least three possibilities:

### A. True removal

The distinction is no longer required.

### B. Representation compression

The distinction remains semantically recoverable from other components.

### C. Semantic reclassification

Two previously separate dimensions are discovered to represent one underlying distinction.

Therefore:

$$
\boxed{
\text{dimension reduction}
\neq
\text{information deletion}.
}
$$

This is exactly where today's **eliminability vs preservation vs realization** distinction becomes useful. 

