## My overall verdict

**Yes, there is a very strong connection with today's research.**

In fact, I think the new document has accidentally arrived at the **concrete representation problem that D4.5 was built to formalize**.

But we should make one fundamental methodological reversal:

> **Do not start from an infinite-dimensional knowledge space and derive observations from it. Start from required distinctions and admissible observations, derive the quotient, and then investigate whether an evolving-dimensional representation emerges.**

So:

$$
\boxed{
\text{D4.5 does not validate }\mathcal K_\infty.
}
$$

Rather:

$$
\boxed{
\text{D4.5 gives us the machinery to test whether an evolving }\mathcal K_\infty
